        "text_zNBFjf": {
          "type": "text",
          "name": "t:names.text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Natural pearls are formed inside oysters; pearls are carefully selected for their luster, smoothness, and radiant glow, and skilled artisans delicately craft them into necklaces, earrings, and ornaments that reflect timeless refinement. Pearl jewellery is one of the most timeless forms of adornment. Unlike most gemstones mined from the earth, pearls are organic gems formed inside living mollusks. Their soft glow and elegance have made them symbols of purity, sophistication, and beauty. Pearls have been treasured for thousands of years and were historically rare because they had to be discovered naturally in oceans and rivers. Common types include natural pearls, cultured pearls, freshwater pearls, and saltwater pearls. Pearls are associated with purity, wisdom, femininity, and prosperity. Creating pearl jewellery involves sorting pearls by size and luster, drilling them, and arranging them carefully into harmonious designs.</p>",
