        "text_cwCTiB": {
          "type": "text",
          "name": "t:names.text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Historians suggest Maharani Aijabde Punwar was the first woman to wear silver replica jewellery as a symbol of honor, elegance, and devotion. Silver replica jewellery refers to ornaments crafted to resemble traditional silver jewellery while being more affordable and accessible. These pieces are inspired by historic ornamental styles and traditional craftsmanship. Artisans began recreating elaborate silver ornaments using affordable metals so more people could enjoy traditional jewellery designs. Replica jewellery is usually made from metals such as brass, alloy, or copper. The metal is shaped through casting or molding, detailed with engraving or decorative motifs, and finished with oxidized or polished surfaces to resemble silver. Silver replica jewellery represents heritage, elegance, and cultural artistry while allowing traditional styles to remain widely accessible. Today these ornaments are popular for daily fashion, festivals, weddings, and designer collections inspired by traditional jewellery styles.<br/><br/></p>",
            "width": "100%",
