        "text_LgqPza": {
          "type": "text",
          "name": "t:names.text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Moissanite jewellery is made using moissanite, a gemstone composed of silicon carbide known for its exceptional brilliance and durability. It was first discovered in 1893 by French scientist Henri Moissan in a meteor crater in Arizona, USA. Because natural moissanite is extremely rare, most jewellery today uses lab-created moissanite stones. In India, moissanite jewellery became widely available through the gemstone manufacturing industry in Surat, Gujarat, which is known globally for diamond cutting and polishing. Unlike traditional gemstones, moissanite jewellery was not popularized by any historical Indian king, as it is a modern gemstone used mainly in contemporary jewellery design.<br/><br/></p>",
            "width": "100%",
