        "text_reitCM": {
          "type": "text",
          "name": "t:names.text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Shell jewellery is one of the oldest forms of adornment in human history and originated in coastal regions of Africa, the Mediterranean, and Southeast Asia thousands of years ago. Archaeological discoveries show that shells were used for ornaments as early as 100,000 years ago. In India, shell jewellery became popular in coastal regions and evidence of shell ornaments also appears in the Indus Valley Civilization. Artisans collect natural seashells, clean and polish them, and then cut, carve, or drill them to create beads, pendants, bangles, and decorative ornaments. Shells symbolize fertility, prosperity, protection, and feminine energy in many cultures. Their natural shapes, textures, and colours allow artisans to create unique and creative jewellery designs. Today, shell jewellery is admired for its natural beauty, eco friendly nature, and lightweight comfort.<br/></p>",
