            "text": "<p>Nano setting jewellery is a modern jewellery technique in which extremely small gemstones are placed very closely together using microscopic precision tools. The stones are set with minimal visible metal, creating a continuous sparkling surface. This advanced technique developed in modern jewellery manufacturing technology in the late 20th and early 21st centuries. Nano setting jewellery became popular through the advanced jewellery manufacturing centers. Today it is widely used in moissanite, diamond, and fashion jewellery designs for its brilliant and elegant appearance.<br/></p>",
