        "text_zqUWVP": {
          "type": "text",
          "name": "t:names.text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>India witnessed the birth of Kundan jewellery during the glorious Mughal era in the late 16th century. The imperial ateliers of Delhi and Agra nurtured this refined art form, and later Rajasthan and Gujarat became major centers of its fame. Jaipur artisans perfected its luxurious gemstone-setting craft over centuries. Kundan is renowned for its pure gold foil technique that delicately embraces uncut stones, involving the layering and pressing of highly refined gold around each gemstone. Traditional methods avoid modern machines, preserving authentic craftsmanship, as expert karigars carefully shape, polish, and set every stone by hand. The reverse side often features vibrant Meenakari enamel artistry, while large uncut gems create a bold, regal, and majestic appearance. Design inspirations reflect Mughal architecture, floral gardens, and palace elegance. Each masterpiece demands patience, precision, and years of experience, with generations of artisan families proudly passing down this treasured skill. Kundan jewellery symbolizes luxury, heritage, and timeless beauty, remaining a cherished choice for Indian bridal and festive attire. Add Kundan to your collection to embrace centuries of royal elegance and unmatched grace.<br/><br/></p>",
